# Automatic Post-Change Validation

After completing any of these tasks, run the `post-change-validation` skill **before** reporting done to the user:

- Refactoring (rename, extract, move, inline, delete) touching 2+ files
- Adding or removing a feature, view, service, or model
- Changing a service API (method signature, return type, parameters)
- Deleting files or folders
- Adding/removing enum cases

Skip validation for trivial changes (single-line fix, comment edit, token swap).

## How to Run

1. Identify changed files via `git diff --name-only` or from the edits you just made
2. Follow the full checklist in the `post-change-validation` skill
3. Report findings inline — do not ask the user whether to validate, just do it
4. If findings exist, fix them before reporting done (or flag items that need user decision)
